<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Drevlians</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 946 CE (approx.) · capital Iskorosten</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Forest-dwelling East Slavs west of Kiev who killed Prince Igor in 945 and suffered the ferocious revenge of his widow Olga.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Drevlians, the people of the trees, lived in the forests between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pripyat-river">Pripyat</a> and the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, west of the Polans. They appear in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> as an old tribe with their own princes and their chief town at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korosten">Iskorosten</a>, modern Korosten in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were farmers, hunters and beekeepers, and the Kievan chronicler, hostile to them, describes them as living in a bestial way. After Oleg subdued them, in 883 according to the chronicle, they paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>. In 945 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igor-svyatoslavich">Prince Igor</a> tried to collect a second tribute, and the Drevlians under their prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mal-of-the-drevlians">Mal</a> killed him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igor-of-kiev">Igor</a>'s widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olga-of-kiev">Olga</a> took vengeance in 946, burying and burning Drevlian envoys and setting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korosten">Iskorosten</a> alight with birds carrying burning tinder. The Drevlian land was then ruled directly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, and in 970 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav I</a> gave it to his son Oleg. The tribe merged into the population of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/drevlians.jpg" alt="Drevlians" width="320" height="398"><figcaption>Image: SeikoEn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Slavic_tribes_peoples_8th_9th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 946 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Iskorosten</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Derevlians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=773&amp;focus=drevlians" aria-label="Drevlians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5331 411 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Drevlians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5651 667L5697 681"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5697 681h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5651 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5651 667h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Iskorosten. <a href="/atlas?year=773&amp;focus=drevlians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

